WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:05.480
Tell us a little bit about going to the [1944] Orange Bowl your freshman year.

2
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.260
Oh, what a great trip that was.

3
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:16.240
That was really magnificent and . . . We played Texas A&amp;M in the Orange Bowl.

4
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:26.980
Texas A&amp;M . . . I had three or four buddies that I knew before I went to LSU that went to A&amp;M.

5
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:32.040
And we kidded each other real harshly, you know.

6
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.060
We . . . It was all in fun,

7
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:50.240
but we kidded each other about the spirit of competitiveness between Texas A&amp;M and LSU, which still exists today.

8
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:55.140
And I . . . If I wrote him a letter, I would tell him things like, well,

9
00:00:55.140 --> 00:01:04.920
“You sloppy guys over there,” and, “You’re not getting an education, you’re getting a free ride,” joking, of course.

10
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.060
And they’d do the same thing for me.

11
00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:09.960
But we were . . . We were real close friends.

12
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:16.280
And so when we wound up be . . . winning our conference and they won their conference,

13
00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:22.340
and we wound up in the Orange Bowl, I . . . We had to win.

14
00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:23.820
That’s all there was to it.

15
00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:25.220
We had to beat A&amp;M.

16
00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.460
And we beat ’em good. [laughter]

17
00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.100
Okay.

18
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.560
You’ve got to tell us a little bit about the game itself.

19
00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.900
The game was a great game.

20
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.580
I don’t remember the exact score but I think we won . . .

21
00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.608
Let me see.

22
00:01:41.608 --> 00:01:42.960
. . . fourteen.

23
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.180
Yeah, she’s got the record . . .

24
00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:44.620
It’s on the banner.

25
00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.020
. . . so there’s no need to be guessing.

26
00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.560
But it was a low-scoring game.

27
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.940
And we had Y.A.

28
00:01:50.940 --> 00:02:00.280
Tittle and Jimmy Cason and Charlie Barney, who played a lot of the time, not all of the time.

29
00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:01.780
Joe Reid.

30
00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:08.100
Quite a few prominent, later professional players.

31
00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:16.840
And we beat them Aggies! [all laugh] And I think that it was a good game.

32
00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:24.200
I think, I don’t know, the score may have been twelve or fourteen to seven, or something like that.

33
00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:24.880
It was very good.

34
00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:26.720
So it was a defensive struggle, then, if it was . . . ?

35
00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.500
Quite a bit.

36
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:36.860
Quite a bit, yeah, which was unusual for us because we had some great offensive players in Y.A.

37
00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:39.000
Tittle and Steve Van Buren.

38
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.260
We made the . . . We had to go all the way down the field and we made a touchdown.

39
00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.140
What kind of . . . Was it a running or a passing?

40
00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.160
Passing, primarily.

41
00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:47.400
Y.A.

42
00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.940
Tittle and his passing and . . . Oh, no, no, no. Steve ran quite a bit of that.

43
00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:52.720
So it was both.

44
00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:53.340
It was a mixture.

45
00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.120
So he ran it to get down there, and then maybe it was a pass to get in the end zone?

46
00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:02.380
Well, it took . . . probably took five minutes of play to do . . . to win the game.

47
00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:08.480
And in five minutes, you can do a lot of . . . run a lot of different plays, you know.

48
00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.460
But, anyway, that’s . . . We won it.

49
00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.280
We won the game [all laughing].

50
00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.320
We beat them Aggies.

51
00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:17.440
Well how did you . . . How did you celebrate?

52
00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.540
Oh, boy. [laughs] We really celebrated.

53
00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.020
I hate . . .

54
00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.820
Anything you can tell?

55
00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.160
No?

56
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:24.393
Okay.

57
00:03:24.393 --> 00:03:31.660
No. There’s nothing that . . . We went back to . . . We went back to Baton Rouge immediately.

58
00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:37.820
I think we went back on the train that night, so we didn’t do any celebrating.

59
00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:43.640
But when we got back to Baton Rouge, we did some celebrating.

60
00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.680
We really did it well.

61
00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:46.580
We enjoyed it.

62
00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.920
It was fun.

63
00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:52.340
And we had a crowd meeting us at the train station.

64
00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:57.340
And, you know, it was . . . It was inspirational.

65
00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:58.360
It was very nice.
